; Test: Non-determinism with MaxSink when priorities are equal
; Question: When multiple exec rules have the SAME priority, what happens?
; In PathMap, items are stored in byte-order of their full expression.

; Setup: Multiple max sinks with SAME priority (0) but different patterns
; This creates non-determinism - which one fires first?

(data 5)
(data 3)
(data 8)
(data 1)

; All three exec rules have priority 0
; Question: Which max gets computed first? Does order matter?

(exec 0
  (, (data $x))
  (O (max (max-a $m) $m $x)))

(exec 0
  (, (data $y))
  (O (max (max-b $m) $m $y)))

(exec 0
  (, (data $z))
  (O (max (max-c $m) $m $z)))

; Expected: All three should produce the same max value (8)
; But which appears first in the output?
; Answer: Depends on byte-order of the full exec expression
;
; Hypothesis: Since all have priority 0, PathMap orders by:
; 1. Priority bytes (same for all: 0)
; 2. Pattern bytes (different: max-a, max-b, max-c)
; 3. Lexicographic on pattern → max-a < max-b < max-c
;
; So expected order: (max-a 8) (max-b 8) (max-c 8)
